<title>CHINA: Quake shakes China's Tibet region.</title>
<headline>Quake shakes China's Tibet region.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>An earthquake measuring 5.0 on the open-ended Richter scale shook a remote corner of China's Tibetan region on Monday, the official Xinhua news agency said.</p>
<p>The quake was centred in the Naqu region, about 600 km (360 miles) northwest of the regional capital, Lhasa.</p>
<p>There were no immediate reports of injuries or damage and the mountainous region is thinly populated.</p>
</text>
